        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 344,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000237
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-28T20:29:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two trigger points for device to move from DOWNLOAD_IMAGE state back to ENABLE state: \n\none is when user issues the get_image_download_status and receives DOWNLOAD_SUCCEEDED or DOWNLOAD_FAILED; \n\nthe other is when the adapter receives download completion notification from device, the adapter will change the device state to ENABLE.\n\nIn both cases, it is each adapter\u0027s responsibility to do the transition. \n\nI don\u0027t think we allow the user to change device state when it is in DOWNLOAD_IMAGE state. There is assertion check in local_handler that allows the user to disable a device only when it is in enabled state.",
      "parentUuid": "5a202591_afe1459c",
      "revId": "65e9c75aff8acd762340c5e07df15807834a18b2",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
